{title: 112 - Let Us With a Gladsome Mind}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #112 • MONKLAND • 7s}
{lyricist: John Milton}
{composer: John Antes}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 112}
{meta: tune MONKLAND}
{meta: meter 7s}
{meta: category God the Father - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Gm/D]Let us [Dm/A]with agladsome [Eb]mind
[Bb]Praise [Eb]the [Adim]Lord, [Bb]for [F/C]He [Cm]is [Dm/A]kind:
[Adim]For [Gm]His mercies [F7/Eb]shall [Bb]endure,
[Bb]Ever faithful, ever [F]sure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm/D]He, with [Dm/A]all commanding [Eb]might,
[Bb]Filled [Eb]the [Adim]new [Bb]made [F/C]world [Cm]with [Dm/A]light:
[Adim]For [Gm]His mercies [F7/Eb]shall [Bb]endure,
[Bb]Ever faithful, ever [F]sure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Gm/D]All things [Dm/A]living [Gm]He [Eb]does feed;
[Bb]His [Eb]full [Adim]hand [Bb]supplies [Cm]their [Dm/A]need:
[Adim]For [Gm]His mercies [F7/Eb]shall [Bb]endure,
[Bb]Ever faithful, ever [F]sure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Gm/D]Let us [Dm/A]then with [Gm]gladsome [Eb]mind
[Bb]Praise [Eb]the [Adim]Lord, [Bb]for [F/C]He [Cm]is [Dm/A]kind:
[Adim]For [Gm]His mercies [F7/Eb]shall [Bb]endure,
[Bb]Ever faithful, ever [F]sure.
{end_of_verse}
